  "description": "A parametric RECEPTION DESK on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nDROP IT ON A NODE. The visitor faces the −v side: a timber cubby wall rises to the transaction ledge (worktop + ledge rise), and a white fascia sweeps across it from full height at one end down to Sweep low point at the other — a cosine, so it leaves the top and arrives at the floor tangentially. The staff worktop sits behind at worktop height between two white end panels.\n\nDEFAULTS are the INFRA Reception dims sheet (slide 16): 3300 long, 800 deep, 750 worktop, 300 ledge rise.\n\nWHAT THIS CANNOT DO: the reference fascia is a doubly-curved solid; this one is a vertical ribbon of flat segments whose top edge follows the curve.",
